WEBVTT

00:00:15.450 --> 00:00:18.370
Huh? Kikko, you read boys' comics?

00:00:18.410 --> 00:00:20.450
No, I was just bored.

00:00:20.830 --> 00:00:22.290
Here. Espresso con panna.

00:00:22.330 --> 00:00:23.460
Oh, yes.

00:00:37.250 --> 00:00:39.370
Here is your espresso con panna.

00:00:40.080 --> 00:00:41.450
Please enjoy.

00:00:45.500 --> 00:00:47.250
Um, excuse me.

00:00:47.330 --> 00:00:48.370
Yes?

00:00:50.000 --> 00:00:52.030
You are Kikko Hoshino, right?

00:00:53.160 --> 00:00:54.540
Well, yes.

00:00:56.250 --> 00:00:59.530
My name is Jiro Hitoyoshi.
 I need your help.

00:00:59.540 --> 00:01:02.040
(July, the 41st of Shinka Era. Ginza)

00:01:16.580 --> 00:01:19.040
Senpai. Jiro Senpai!

00:01:26.810 --> 00:01:29.620
Fuurouta, don't be so angry.

00:01:31.540 --> 00:01:33.190
Watch your mouth, Hitoyoshi.

00:01:53.920 --> 00:01:54.960
Miss Kikko!

00:02:01.040 --> 00:02:03.680
Mr. Jiro! I am 20 years old now.

00:02:14.750 --> 00:02:17.000
- No, Miss Kikko.
 - Let go!

00:02:17.080 --> 00:02:18.870
What, superhumans?

00:02:19.080 --> 00:02:20.490
Fight elsewhere!

00:02:20.750 --> 00:02:21.950
It causes problems.

00:02:22.000 --> 00:02:24.120
I will definitely catch him.

00:02:32.000 --> 00:02:36.010
(Love is to Never Regret)

00:02:36.000 --> 00:02:38.970
(April, the 46th of Shinka Era.
 Shinjuku)

00:02:59.910 --> 00:03:04.660
I heard it
 A voice cursing fate

00:03:05.030 --> 00:03:08.620
I found it
 A way to use my power

00:03:08.790 --> 00:03:12.540
What you want are not words,
 are they?

00:03:12.540 --> 00:03:16.250
That love inside
 I want to send it on

00:03:16.500 --> 00:03:18.630
Justice is not on my side

00:03:18.630 --> 00:03:23.590
The only thing absolute for me
 is myself

00:03:23.870 --> 00:03:25.290
Come on Wakers. Ready, go!

00:03:25.330 --> 00:03:30.500
Protecting the illusions
 that somebody dreamed of

00:03:30.700 --> 00:03:34.700
will liberate the stagnant sky

00:03:35.410 --> 00:03:40.540
We hurl our unanswerable cries
 at each other

00:03:40.830 --> 00:03:45.700
And they become the reason we live

00:03:46.120 --> 00:03:51.450
What can I do in this
 hopeless world we live in?

00:03:51.500 --> 00:03:56.410
Only those that keep searching

00:03:56.540 --> 00:03:59.040
can become the future

00:03:59.120 --> 00:04:04.200
Start the revolution!

00:04:09.580 --> 00:04:12.330
One of
 the 12 constellations of the Zodiac.

00:04:12.370 --> 00:04:16.200
Along with the Summer Triangle,
 it's a famous summer constellation.

00:04:16.250 --> 00:04:18.330
Scorpio. It's coming into view.

00:04:18.450 --> 00:04:22.250
Around it, a celestial body Exeter
 that emits strong x-rays

00:04:22.290 --> 00:04:24.540
has recently been discovered.

00:04:24.990 --> 00:04:28.790
While scholars around the world
 pursue its accurate position,

00:04:28.830 --> 00:04:34.000
it is said Japan's Prof. Onda finally
 succeeded in fixing the coordinates.

00:04:34.330 --> 00:04:38.160
A certain group has been approaching
 this Prof. Onda these few days.

00:04:38.200 --> 00:04:39.950
Hello, Prof. Onda.

00:04:41.000 --> 00:04:42.370
Keep it down.

00:04:45.500 --> 00:04:47.180
Here, the item we promised you.

00:04:48.660 --> 00:04:50.770
You know industrial spies, right?

00:04:51.450 --> 00:04:55.520
Rivaling companies try to steal
 each others' technology, right?

00:04:56.660 --> 00:04:59.660
A transaction is about
 to be made here.

00:04:59.910 --> 00:05:03.950
Japan's leading scientist is about to
 sell off certain information.

00:05:06.080 --> 00:05:07.950
What happens if it's sold?

00:05:09.080 --> 00:05:13.450
Japan, no, the world's scientific
 advances will be delayed 10 years.

00:05:14.040 --> 00:05:17.410
Industrial spies are trying
 to steal our future.

00:05:17.790 --> 00:05:19.840
You'll really do it, Hoshinoko?

00:05:23.760 --> 00:05:26.330
Why help a stranger...?

00:05:34.000 --> 00:05:36.450
But it's for this planet...

00:05:51.700 --> 00:05:55.000
So this man is
 Japan's leading scientist.

00:05:55.830 --> 00:05:57.620
And he's an industrial spy.

00:05:58.370 --> 00:06:00.330
He's a bad guy.

00:06:01.950 --> 00:06:03.580
Please, enjoy.

00:06:04.750 --> 00:06:05.790
Well then.

00:06:05.830 --> 00:06:07.580
Here is the item I promised you.

00:06:07.660 --> 00:06:09.220
Great, thank you.

00:06:09.750 --> 00:06:12.450
So this is the newest collimator?

00:06:12.540 --> 00:06:15.100
I can finally locate Scorpio Exeter.

00:06:15.290 --> 00:06:18.370
Huh?
 It's the opposite of what I heard.

00:06:18.410 --> 00:06:20.980
I thought the professor
 was selling info.

00:06:23.250 --> 00:06:24.660
What is going on?

00:06:24.750 --> 00:06:28.410
Wasn't Prof. Onda selling
 the x-ray source coordinates?

00:06:28.700 --> 00:06:29.820
What should I do?

00:06:32.950 --> 00:06:36.330
You're a savior of
 Japan's astronomical studies.

00:06:36.790 --> 00:06:39.700
I want to test it right now. Goodbye.

00:06:50.370 --> 00:06:51.300
What?

00:06:51.500 --> 00:06:52.550
Um...!

00:06:52.950 --> 00:06:55.450
I will take the check, young lady.

00:06:55.910 --> 00:06:57.620
- Kikko?
 - What is it?

00:06:57.700 --> 00:06:59.830
What are you doing, Kikko?

00:07:00.080 --> 00:07:01.580
Forgive me, sir.

00:07:02.160 --> 00:07:03.150
Grab it, Kikko!

00:07:06.250 --> 00:07:07.370
Darn!

00:07:07.910 --> 00:07:08.910
Sleep!

00:07:20.620 --> 00:07:22.460
A spy from another planet, huh?

00:07:24.330 --> 00:07:25.370
No.

00:07:25.410 --> 00:07:26.580
Kikko, are you...?

00:07:27.700 --> 00:07:29.080
No I am not!

00:07:49.500 --> 00:07:52.790
We have to, Hoshinoko.
 Set the witch power's channel.

00:07:52.830 --> 00:07:54.370
Huh? Are you sure?

00:07:54.410 --> 00:07:57.490
Better than standing out and
 getting caught by journalists.

00:07:58.000 --> 00:08:00.250
Who knows what layer
 you'll be sent to next?

00:08:02.750 --> 00:08:04.200
Meteortail!

00:09:11.870 --> 00:09:14.950
It's a witch girl. Right?

00:09:21.500 --> 00:09:22.830
Hey. Where is it?

00:09:23.750 --> 00:09:25.710
Oh... Here.

00:09:41.200 --> 00:09:42.410
Is that...?

00:09:42.910 --> 00:09:44.700
An "S" Planetarian.

00:09:51.330 --> 00:09:52.330
Um.

00:09:52.500 --> 00:09:55.080
I'd like to let people in now.

00:09:55.200 --> 00:09:57.700
I am sorry. Just a bit longer.

00:09:58.750 --> 00:10:01.950
The Super Population
 Research Laboratory?

00:10:02.000 --> 00:10:03.330
What is that?

00:10:03.540 --> 00:10:05.410
Of the Health and Welfare Ministry.

00:10:05.450 --> 00:10:08.250
You can check with the government
 if you like.

00:10:08.410 --> 00:10:11.910
Oh, here it comes. Just as planned.

00:10:21.830 --> 00:10:24.720
It's Grosse Augen!
 It's on the humans' side.

00:10:26.330 --> 00:10:28.620
It came to fight the evil alien?

00:10:43.950 --> 00:10:45.950
- It disappeared.
 - What?

00:10:46.500 --> 00:10:48.080
I'll go this way.

00:10:48.660 --> 00:10:50.830
It disappeared. Like always.

00:10:50.830 --> 00:10:53.200
But I am counting on you today.

00:10:53.290 --> 00:10:54.580
I know.

00:11:13.910 --> 00:11:16.030
I need your help a bit more.

00:11:16.450 --> 00:11:19.080
Mr. Hitoyoshi,
 you knew the spy was an alien.

00:11:19.120 --> 00:11:20.250
I did.

00:11:20.540 --> 00:11:22.790
And you're the witch girl of rumors.

00:11:23.450 --> 00:11:26.750
No, wait. I don't know
 what you're talking about.

00:11:26.790 --> 00:11:28.000
Tell me, Kikko.

00:11:28.000 --> 00:11:29.660
You called me that again.

00:11:29.910 --> 00:11:30.870
What?

00:11:32.000 --> 00:11:36.000
People don't call me by my name,
 so it's embarrassing.

00:11:36.080 --> 00:11:40.130
And I didn't know what to do,
 so I used magic.

00:11:41.330 --> 00:11:43.140
Sorry, I won't do it again.

00:11:43.140 --> 00:11:45.890
- No, you can...
 - Look.

00:11:51.290 --> 00:11:54.500
It's that alien and Grosse Augen.

00:11:54.580 --> 00:11:56.620
You know Grosse Augen?

00:11:56.660 --> 00:12:00.750
I saw it in a magazine.
 The heroic superhuman was real, huh?

00:12:01.290 --> 00:12:03.950
Grosse Augen, our ally, huh?

00:12:04.450 --> 00:12:06.450
Tell me its accurate position.

00:12:06.660 --> 00:12:08.750
What? You can't see it?

00:12:08.910 --> 00:12:10.660
I am a regular human.

00:12:11.160 --> 00:12:15.660
When Grosse Augen becomes giant,
 it shifts the temporal phase nearby.

00:12:16.040 --> 00:12:17.950
Temporal phase? What?

00:12:18.410 --> 00:12:20.330
The Fred and Hoyle effect.

00:12:20.370 --> 00:12:21.970
Like movie films.

00:12:22.620 --> 00:12:25.750
Each frame is the time
 we can recognize.

00:12:26.120 --> 00:12:30.040
But in reality, there is more time
 in between each frame.

00:12:30.830 --> 00:12:35.410
A gap in time that's right there,
 but is not visible or tangible.

00:12:36.000 --> 00:12:39.570
Grosse Augen goes in that gap
 to hide from us.

00:12:39.790 --> 00:12:44.540
Maybe it's being considerate
 as to not spread the damage.

00:12:44.660 --> 00:12:48.870
Who knows? This machine has
 an observation mechanism, but...

00:12:50.750 --> 00:12:53.250
I cannot read this while driving.

00:12:53.620 --> 00:12:56.040
Actually, I don't know how to.

00:12:58.700 --> 00:13:00.700
And who are you people?

00:13:01.500 --> 00:13:03.590
Superhumans protect
 the peace of humans.

00:13:04.330 --> 00:13:06.720
Then who protects superhumans?

00:13:07.830 --> 00:13:11.470
Superhumans hide their identity
 and live among humans.

00:13:12.450 --> 00:13:14.540
We protect those superhumans.

00:13:15.040 --> 00:13:19.150
So you don't have to keep
 changing jobs and boarding places.

00:13:21.910 --> 00:13:24.110
You can do it, Grosse Augen.

00:13:24.660 --> 00:13:26.540
The evil alien is over there.

00:13:26.910 --> 00:13:28.370
That way.

00:13:29.000 --> 00:13:30.160
All right.

00:13:30.160 --> 00:13:31.910
Lift your head, Equus.

00:13:38.450 --> 00:13:39.620
What is that?

00:13:41.290 --> 00:13:42.620
An iron horse?

00:13:43.080 --> 00:13:44.080
Which way?

00:13:46.910 --> 00:13:48.040
This way?

00:14:02.370 --> 00:14:04.530
Not here, over there!

00:14:04.750 --> 00:14:06.620
You're in the way, witch girl.

00:14:06.900 --> 00:14:08.410
In the way?

00:14:10.830 --> 00:14:14.540
Earthling.
 I won't let you ruin our plan.

00:14:14.540 --> 00:14:18.040
You just do your invasion plan
 or whatever.

00:14:23.250 --> 00:14:24.550
Watch out!

00:14:24.910 --> 00:14:29.370
That's a heat wave attack, so changing
 the air into a lens is worse.

00:14:29.410 --> 00:14:32.750
An answer like that will
 fail your next test too.

00:14:32.790 --> 00:14:35.080
Don't say that now.

00:14:35.060 --> 00:14:36.580
I got it, water!

00:14:37.580 --> 00:14:38.830
Mr. Cloud.

00:14:45.910 --> 00:14:47.870
Bye!

00:14:48.370 --> 00:14:51.700
Controlling the atmosphere?
 What technology.

00:14:52.080 --> 00:14:53.830
It's just plain magic.

00:14:59.450 --> 00:15:00.370
Too bad.

00:15:00.410 --> 00:15:03.200
Since I see you this much,
 I can't let you go.

00:15:42.160 --> 00:15:43.540
What are you doing?

00:15:44.040 --> 00:15:46.450
I told you,
 Grosse Augen is on our side.

00:15:46.500 --> 00:15:48.760
Earth's ally, a heroic superhuman.

00:16:04.750 --> 00:16:06.660
Hey, where are you going?

00:16:10.160 --> 00:16:11.620
Why?

00:16:11.870 --> 00:16:14.580
Why did you attack Grosse Augen?

00:16:26.120 --> 00:16:29.290
Why? Why are Jiro Senpai and I...?

00:16:29.370 --> 00:16:31.330
Got tracked by a dog, huh?

00:16:49.120 --> 00:16:53.120
That's the body fluid of
 a monster called Nuppepoo.

00:16:53.870 --> 00:16:55.750
Don't feel anything, right?

00:16:55.790 --> 00:16:59.620
But to me, it smells so good.

00:16:59.830 --> 00:17:02.750
So no matter how far you are,
 I can smell you.

00:17:03.290 --> 00:17:04.290
Grosse Augen.

00:17:05.580 --> 00:17:06.660
Grosse Augen?

00:17:06.750 --> 00:17:10.120
You have forcibly possessed
 a human's body.

00:17:10.160 --> 00:17:13.910
Because of that,
 your bodies are close to the limit.

00:17:18.200 --> 00:17:19.540
Maruya's back door.

00:17:24.830 --> 00:17:26.790
Is he really Grosse Augen?

00:17:33.750 --> 00:17:37.040
Grosse Augen,
 separate from that human. Or else...

00:17:37.080 --> 00:17:38.250
Hear me out.

00:17:38.410 --> 00:17:40.290
I cannot separate from him.

00:17:40.450 --> 00:17:43.330
We share a life now.

00:17:51.080 --> 00:17:53.210
I could tell he was about to die.

00:17:54.000 --> 00:17:56.290
There was only one way to save him.

00:17:56.330 --> 00:17:58.620
His soul spoke to me.

00:17:59.080 --> 00:18:00.830
I answered right away.

00:18:00.910 --> 00:18:03.870
"Fine. I will give you my life."

00:18:04.540 --> 00:18:08.000
But in exchange,
 in order to save this planet,

00:18:08.080 --> 00:18:10.410
fight with me.

00:18:12.330 --> 00:18:17.330
But you could say that Grosse Augen,
 a monster, took over your body.

00:18:18.000 --> 00:18:20.580
Your existences are
 unstable, dangerous.

00:18:20.570 --> 00:18:21.870
But why?

00:18:21.950 --> 00:18:26.040
Grosse Augen has fought evil aliens
 like that in the past.

00:18:26.620 --> 00:18:27.660
Thanks.

00:18:28.120 --> 00:18:29.120
I understand.

00:18:29.580 --> 00:18:32.750
But I have given my life
 to Grosse Augen.

00:18:33.250 --> 00:18:35.410
I want to keep that promise.

00:18:35.660 --> 00:18:38.330
If you give your life,
 you cannot exist.

00:18:38.410 --> 00:18:40.750
Don't say you don't mind dying.

00:18:41.750 --> 00:18:44.410
Grosse Augen's body is at its limit.

00:18:44.790 --> 00:18:47.270
Now, he can still
 go back to his homeland.

00:18:57.080 --> 00:18:58.540
Wait, there must be a way.

00:18:58.580 --> 00:18:59.750
Don't come.

00:19:04.540 --> 00:19:05.540
No, Kikko.

00:19:05.750 --> 00:19:08.870
Magic that deals
 with human lives is forbidden.

00:19:08.910 --> 00:19:12.000
I know. I know, but...

00:19:24.160 --> 00:19:25.540
Farewell, Grosse Augen.

00:19:26.160 --> 00:19:28.750
We will never forget you, huh?

00:19:29.750 --> 00:19:30.950
Where is he?

00:19:35.200 --> 00:19:36.830
He was long dead.

00:19:36.870 --> 00:19:39.910
Why? You said you
 protected superhumans.

00:19:40.950 --> 00:19:43.080
I dispose of dangerous superhumans.

00:19:43.250 --> 00:19:44.830
That's my job too.

00:19:46.040 --> 00:19:48.120
Due to the Gemini Accident
 in America,

00:19:48.160 --> 00:19:51.160
we can't get the collimator data.

00:19:51.540 --> 00:19:55.830
Then they said they would provide me
 with the latest version.

00:19:56.290 --> 00:19:58.410
I can't believe they were aliens.

00:19:58.950 --> 00:20:03.000
The Gemini Accident was probably
 caused by an "S" Planetarian too.

00:20:03.370 --> 00:20:04.290
Watch this.

00:20:07.040 --> 00:20:11.620
It catches the x-ray source more
 accurately than any Earth technology.

00:20:12.040 --> 00:20:13.120
However...

00:20:14.620 --> 00:20:19.620
Like this, anyone can freely change
 the data with external radio waves.

00:20:19.830 --> 00:20:22.070
But what for?

00:20:22.540 --> 00:20:26.330
Thank you for your work.
 Good luck with your research.

00:20:27.120 --> 00:20:30.080
But watch out for evil aliens.

00:20:30.500 --> 00:20:34.080
So instead of buying information,
 it was the opposite.

00:20:34.660 --> 00:20:39.000
But we succeeded in luring
 Grosse Augen to confirm its identity.

00:20:39.160 --> 00:20:40.160
Don't complain.

00:20:40.200 --> 00:20:43.580
In the planet they call Scorpio-X1,

00:20:43.660 --> 00:20:46.660
they say there's
 an "S" Planetarian base.

00:20:46.750 --> 00:20:49.450
They probably didn't want that found.

00:20:52.330 --> 00:20:53.350
Oh.

00:20:53.620 --> 00:20:55.290
Ah, you're here.

00:20:56.080 --> 00:20:57.540
What is this place?

00:20:57.910 --> 00:20:58.900
The Superhuman Bureau.

00:21:00.330 --> 00:21:03.160
A group that protects
 and manages superhumans.

00:21:03.200 --> 00:21:05.790
Starting today, you're a member.

00:21:11.450 --> 00:21:12.870
You are Grosse Augen.

00:21:14.080 --> 00:21:15.120
But...

00:21:28.950 --> 00:21:30.250
That day...

00:21:30.330 --> 00:21:33.620
In exchange for separating me
 from Grosse Augen,

00:21:33.660 --> 00:21:37.190
he let me merge with
 the comatose "S" Planetarian.

00:21:38.580 --> 00:21:41.660
If my heart that loves peace was true,

00:21:41.700 --> 00:21:44.580
I thought I could control
 the "S" Planetarian's mind,

00:21:44.620 --> 00:21:47.750
and become a superhuman of justice.

00:21:49.910 --> 00:21:51.330
Come to think of it...

00:21:51.370 --> 00:21:55.330
There were some reports of
 an "S" Planetarian defeating beasts.

00:21:57.500 --> 00:22:00.120
That day, you disobeyed
 the Superhuman Bureau

00:22:00.160 --> 00:22:02.580
to save that person's life.

00:22:02.660 --> 00:22:04.090
You're really the one I...

00:22:04.080 --> 00:22:06.160
I won't return to
 the Superhuman Bureau.

00:22:12.160 --> 00:22:13.680
Farewell, Kikko.

00:23:56.540 --> 00:23:59.000
Hey guys! You know ghosts, right?

00:23:59.040 --> 00:24:02.000
Monsters, beasts, spirits...
 No, not those.

00:24:02.040 --> 00:24:04.290
Ghosts love to play with kids.

00:24:04.330 --> 00:24:07.790
They're jolly things
 always thinking of pranks.

00:24:07.870 --> 00:24:11.010
I'm Fuurouta the Ghost. Remember me!
